From 296c98afc8ff6bab3fb9eb9eb39c709b1d7bf017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:37:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: OMNI_REF is one pin written three times, so make them
 agree

build.yml, lint.yml and publish.yml each define OMNI_REF, because github
gives workflow files no way to share an `env`. They had two values:

    build.yml    fbf1da64e3c90fc54e3c6b237b0b5835890df8c4
    publish.yml  fbf1da64e3c90fc54e3c6b237b0b5835890df8c4
    lint.yml     064af05a693adfda4400cbdfd85d24d894172da5   <- eight behind

`064af05` is an ancestor of `fbf1da6`, eight omni commits back, so lint was
the stale one and this bumps it to what the other two already use. No other
pin moves: which omni this repository tests against is a deliberate act, and
the comment in build.yml says so.

WHY IT MATTERS. Every port's lint job checks out omni at OMNI_REF and hands
its sources to the linter alongside the tests. A green lint run against one
omni and a green build run against another do not compose into a claim about
either -- the two gates were reading different corpus runners and reporting
one verdict.

publish.yml already states the invariant in writing -- "pinned to the same
commit build.yml checks out" -- and lint.yml drifted anyway, which is what an
invariant stated only in prose is worth. So security.yml's `workflows` job
now fails when the three disagree. It is deliberately a grep rather than a
python tool: it reads the same three lines a person reads, and a disagreement
between workflow files is what that job is already for.

The check was run against the drift it is meant to catch. Before this change
it reports two values and exits 1, naming all three lines; after, it reports
one and passes. `actionlint` with shellcheck is clean across the repository's
workflows.

Both comments now say the pin is one line in three files and that the other
two move with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5zKiMP1i1FRDZ6pzgzrUp
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml    |  5 +++++
 .github/workflows/lint.yml     |  8 +++++++-
 .github/workflows/security.yml | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index e5489d1..110fd6e 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@ env:
   # stays red until re-run, and a green run here is not reproducible from
   # this repo's commit alone. Bump this one line to take a new omni; that
   # bump is the commit CI re-tests every port against.
+  #
+  # AND BUMP THE OTHER TWO WITH IT: lint.yml and publish.yml define OMNI_REF
+  # too, because github gives workflow files no way to share an `env`. It is
+  # one pin written three times. `workflows` in security.yml fails if the
+  # three ever disagree.
   OMNI_REF: fbf1da64e3c90fc54e3c6b237b0b5835890df8c4
 
 jobs:
diff --git a/.github/workflows/lint.yml b/.github/workflows/lint.yml
index bc7296b..d1cb806 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/lint.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/lint.yml
@@ -20,7 +20,13 @@ env:
   # stays red until re-run, and a green run here is not reproducible from
   # this repo's commit alone. Bump this one line to take a new omni; that
   # bump is the commit CI re-tests every port against.
-  OMNI_REF: 064af05a693adfda4400cbdfd85d24d894172da5
+  #
+  # AND BUMP THE OTHER TWO WITH IT. build.yml, lint.yml and publish.yml each
+  # define OMNI_REF -- github gives workflow files no way to share an `env` --
+  # and they are one pin written three times, not three pins. This copy sat
+  # eight omni commits behind the other two and nothing said so, because
+  # nothing looked; security.yml's `workflows` job looks now.
+  OMNI_REF: fbf1da64e3c90fc54e3c6b237b0b5835890df8c4
 
 jobs:
   lint-typescript:
diff --git a/.github/workflows/security.yml b/.github/workflows/security.yml
index 6af6a51..016ed18 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/security.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/security.yml
@@ -82,6 +82,33 @@ jobs:
       - run: |
           go install github.com/rhysd/actionlint/cmd/actionlint@latest
           "$(go env GOPATH)/bin/actionlint"
+      # ONE PIN, WRITTEN THREE TIMES. build.yml, lint.yml and publish.yml each
+      # define OMNI_REF, because github gives workflow files no way to share an
+      # `env`. publish.yml's comment already states the invariant in writing --
+      # "pinned to the same commit build.yml checks out" -- and lint.yml still
+      # drifted eight omni commits behind the other two, which is what an
+      # invariant stated only in prose is worth. A green lint run against one
+      # omni and a green build run against another do not compose into a claim
+      # about either.
+      #
+      # This is deliberately a grep and not a python tool: it reads the same
+      # three lines a person reads, and it lives beside actionlint because a
+      # disagreement between workflow files is exactly what this job is for.
+      - name: OMNI_REF agrees across workflows
+        run: |
+          refs="$(grep -h '^ *OMNI_REF:' .github/workflows/*.yml | awk '{print $2}' | sort -u)"
+          if [ -z "$refs" ]; then
+            echo "no OMNI_REF found in .github/workflows/ -- this check has gone blind"
+            exit 1
+          fi
+          if [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$refs" | wc -l)" -ne 1 ]; then
+            echo "OMNI_REF disagrees across workflows:"
+            grep -n '^ *OMNI_REF:' .github/workflows/*.yml
+            echo
+            echo "They are one pin written three times. Make them equal."
+            exit 1
+          fi
+          echo "OMNI_REF: $refs (all workflows agree)"
 
   shell:
     name: shell lint (shellcheck)
-- 
